        {
          "title": "Styling Mental Model: CSS Modules and Global CSS",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. CSS Modules",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "File named ==*.module.css==, imported as `styles`",
                "Class names are {green:hashed per file}, so they never collide",
                "`styles` keys are the class names; ==camelCase== is easiest to access",
                "Combine classes with a template string or `clsx`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "tsx",
              "lines": [
                "import styles from './x.module.css'",
                "export const Btn = () => (",
                "  <div className={styles.card}>",
                "    <button className={`${styles.btn} ${styles.primary}`} />",
                "  </div>",
                ")"
              ],
              "note": "keys of styles match the class names"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Selector Rules and Global CSS",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A module selector needs at least one ==local class==",
                "Bare `h1 {}` is {red:not allowed}: pair it with a class or use `:global(h1)`",
                "`import './globals.css'` only in root `app/layout.tsx`",
                "Global holds resets, CSS variables, base typography for every route"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Modules vs Global",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Modules",
                "Global CSS"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Scope",
                  "Per component",
                  "Site-wide"
                ],
                [
                  "Works in",
                  "Server and Client Components",
                  "Every route"
                ],
                [
                  "Order",
                  "Independent",
                  "{red:Order-dependent}"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Keep global minimal",
              "text": "Site-wide and order-dependent: use ==Modules== for component styles."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Tailwind Setup and Daily Usage",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Tailwind Setup and Daily Usage",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Install and Load",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`npm i tailwindcss @tailwindcss/postcss postcss`",
                "Add the plugin in `postcss.config.mjs`",
                "v4 loads with one line in `globals.css`: `@import \"tailwindcss\";`",
                "No `tailwind.config.js` or three `@tailwind` directives by default"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "export default {",
                "  plugins: { '@tailwindcss/postcss': {} },",
                "};"
              ],
              "note": "postcss.config.mjs"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Theme and Variants",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==@theme== in CSS adds tokens; `--color-brand` gives `bg-brand` and `text-brand`",
                "Variants stack: `hover:` `focus:` `md:` `dark:`, e.g. `md:flex dark:bg-zinc-900`",
                "Plain CSS with no runtime, so it works in ==Server Components=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "css",
              "lines": [
                "@import \"tailwindcss\";",
                "@theme { --color-brand: #0a7; }"
              ],
              "note": "globals.css"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Static Class Strings",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Class string",
                "Generated?"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Dynamic",
                  "`bg-${color}-500`",
                  "{red:Never}"
                ],
                [
                  "Mapped",
                  "`map[color]` of full names",
                  "{green:Yes}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Scanned, not computed",
              "text": "Tailwind scans source for ==whole class strings==. Map values to full literal names."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "CSS-in-JS and Server Components",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "CSS-in-JS and Server Components",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Why Runtime CSS-in-JS Breaks",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "styled-components, Emotion inject styles via ==context and hooks==",
                "So they work only in ==Client Components==: add `'use client'`",
                "Server Components: no hooks, context or browser APIs",
                "Import one there: {red:fails at build or render}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. SSR Needs a Style Registry",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Render",
                    "sub": "collect styles",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "useServerInsertedHTML",
                    "sub": "flush styles",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "HTML",
                    "sub": "styles arrive first",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Registry lives in a ==client provider== wrapping `children`",
                "Without it: {red:flash of unstyled content}"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Runtime vs Zero-runtime",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Runtime",
                "Zero-runtime"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Examples",
                  "styled-components, Emotion",
                  "CSS Modules, Tailwind, Panda CSS, vanilla-extract"
                ],
                [
                  "CSS made",
                  "by JS in the browser",
                  "==extracted at build time=="
                ],
                [
                  "JS bundle",
                  "heavier",
                  "no styling code"
                ],
                [
                  "Each render",
                  "re-serialises styles",
                  "nothing to redo"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Rule of thumb",
              "text": "New App Router app: ==CSS Modules or Tailwind== for server-rendered UI. Runtime CSS-in-JS only inside isolated client islands."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why does it break in Server Components?** It needs hooks and context.",
                "**How do you stop the SSR flash?** Style registry plus `useServerInsertedHTML`.",
                "**Best default for new projects?** CSS Modules or Tailwind."
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Client State: useState, Context and Zustand",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Client State: useState, Context and Zustand",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Local State and Context",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`useState` is local state, so the component needs ==`'use client'`==",
                "Siblings share it? ==Lift state up== to the nearest common parent",
                "==Context== avoids prop drilling",
                "Provider is a **Client Component** in `layout.tsx`, wrapping `{children}`",
                "Server Components still pass through as `children`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Context re-renders",
              "text": "Every consumer re-renders when the value changes. ==Split contexts== by concern and **memoise** the value object."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Zustand",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "tsx",
              "lines": [
                "const useStore = create((set) => ({",
                "  count: 0,",
                "  inc: () => set(s => ({ count: s.count + 1 })),",
                "}))",
                "const count = useStore(s => s.count)"
              ],
              "note": "selector: re-renders only when that slice changes"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Zustand on the Server",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A module-level store is shared by ==all requests==",
                "It {red:leaks data between users}",
                "Never read the store in Server Components"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "createStore",
                    "sub": "per request",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "useRef",
                    "sub": "inside provider",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Client reads",
                    "sub": "via selector",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "URL Search Params and Theming Without Flash",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "URL Search Params and Theming Without Flash",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. URL State vs useState",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "URL state is ==shareable==, **bookmarkable**, survives refresh and back/forward",
                "{green:URL}: filters, sort, page, tabs",
                "{orange:useState}: modals, input drafts (ephemeral)"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Reading and Writing Params",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "tsx",
              "lines": [
                "export default async function Page({ searchParams }) {",
                "  const { q } = await searchParams",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "server: read from the page prop"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "tsx",
              "lines": [
                "const sp = useSearchParams()",
                "const params = new URLSearchParams(sp)",
                "params.set('page', '2')",
                "router.replace(`?${params}`)"
              ],
              "note": "client: read-only, so copy then write"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`searchParams` is a ==Promise==; using it makes the route **dynamic**",
                "`push` adds a history entry; `replace` does not",
                "`useSearchParams` without ==Suspense== can bail out static rendering of the page"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Theme Without Flash",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Server HTML",
